1
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,080
We're very sorry for the disruption
to your travel plans.

2
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,280
Thank you for your patience and understanding.

3
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,000
No worries.

4
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,880
Ms. Zhang, we apologize for the inconvenience
to your onward journey.

5
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,120
Hello, Ms. Fu.

6
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,079
Thank you so much for your assistance today.

7
00:01:58,079 --> 00:02:01,160
Please accept this fruit platter
with our compliments.

8
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,800
It was my pleasure. You're welcome.

9
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,560
We really appreciate it.

10
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:24,960
Captain, your coffee.

11
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,960
Great. Thanks.

12
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,240
Thank you.

13
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,520
Yu.

14
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,640
Thanks.

15
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,920
- Captain Fan.
- Yes?

16
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:36,159
We received word before takeoff
that the passenger is out of danger.

17
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:40,520
Manager Wang also said
Mr. Fu is treating the whole crew to dinner.

18
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,120
You all worked hard today.
A good meal is well deserved.

19
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,080
Thank you, Captain Fan.

20
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:53,759
Lei, does that mean
our bonus is pretty much in the bag?

21
00:02:53,759 --> 00:02:57,160
Mentor, you were incredible today!

22
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,920
When will I ever be as good as you?

23
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,680
You don't want to be like me.

24
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,200
The best flight is the one
where nothing happens.

25
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,720
[Episode 8]
[Want to Be My Boyfriend Instead?]

26
00:03:22,639 --> 00:03:24,400
Captain Fan, Ruan.

27
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,039
- Come on in.
- I'm waiting for them.

28
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,319
I immediately called the purser.

29
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:28,840
That's when I finally calmed down.

30
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:31,125
- The one who calmed you down was Jiang.
- Mentor.

31
00:03:31,125 --> 00:03:35,000
When it comes to emergencies,
Jiang is the one with real experience.

32
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,480
- Alright. Let's go.
- Let's go.

33
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:38,759
This place is so upscale.
Will we get enough to eat?

34
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:40,651
- Hurry up.
- I'm starving.

35
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:45,840
It's nice and cool.

36
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,920
You're here.

37
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,520
- Mr. Fu.
- Ruan.

38
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,960
You got here early.

39
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,120
When pouring his drink,
my hands were shaking--

40
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,800
Everyone's here.

41
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,945
Come on, grab a seat. Come on.

42
00:04:01,945 --> 00:04:04,759
- We're not late, are we? Let me see...
- No, we were early.

43
00:04:04,759 --> 00:04:05,919
Captain Fan, please.

44
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:07,280
Sit. Ruan, you too.

45
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,040
Sit over here. Come on.

46
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,120
Captain Fan. Thank you.

47
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,960
Take your seats. Don't be shy.

48
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,639
Sit here. Come on.

49
00:04:13,639 --> 00:04:15,160
Here. Come.

50
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,280
- Please, go ahead.
- Everyone, please sit down.

51
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:20,920
Excuse me? We're ready for our food now.

52
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,800
<i>Busy. Handle it yourself.</i>

53
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,519
<i>Alright. Many people came today.</i>

54
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:36,400
All dishes are served. Please enjoy.

55
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,000
Thank you.

56
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,879
Alright, everyone.

57
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:56,199
Before we eat,
let's have Mr. Fu say a few words, shall we?

58
00:04:56,199 --> 00:04:58,160
- Yes, come on.
- Please.

59
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,400
No speeches over dinner.

60
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,000
Or it'll feel like a meeting.

61
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,680
Okay then, how about Captain Fan?

62
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:12,000
Good. Captain Fan, please say something for us.

63
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,720
I'm not talking either.

64
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:17,280
It'll turn into a coordination meeting.

65
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,680
Then...

66
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,640
Ms. Jiang, why don't you say something?

67
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,680
I'll pass.

68
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,600
It'll sound like a briefing. Let's not.

69
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:26,840
Come on, nobody wants to talk?
I can't either. That'd be weird.

70
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,750
Looks like everyone's tense because I'm here.

71
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,840
I don't think you're usually this quiet.

72
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,520
Yeah, you folks are usually pretty lively.

73
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:39,680
- Yeah, we're pretty outgoing.
- Yes, very outgoing.

74
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,043
I want to say something.

75
00:05:43,043 --> 00:05:45,680
Today was my first flight
as the lead attendant.

76
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:49,360
I was already nervous,
and when the accident happened, I just froze.

77
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,280
I don't feel like I contributed much.

78
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,840
Sit down.

79
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:56,120
While we were doing CPR up front,

80
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,720
you were in the back
keeping everyone calm and steady.

81
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,360
That was the biggest help.

82
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:04,065
I almost forgot
it was your first lead attendant flight.

83
00:06:04,065 --> 00:06:05,239
And all of you.

84
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:08,440
Everyone did an amazing job today.

85
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,160
Your scores will definitely be solid.

86
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,400
- Great.
- Good to hear.

87
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,800
I almost forgot.

88
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:19,760
On my first flight as a flight attendant,
Jiang was my purser too.

89
00:06:21,276 --> 00:06:25,480
She always sees the best in people
and lifts them up.

90
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:30,240
Getting Jiang on your first flight
means you're very lucky.

91
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,320
You're making me blush.

92
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,600
Working with all of you is my honor too.

93
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,880
Here's to everyone.

94
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,680
Good.

95
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,320
I was really panicking today.

96
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,630
I was terrified something would go wrong.

97
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:49,279
Otherwise, we'd surely have been punished.

98
00:06:49,279 --> 00:06:50,319
Come on.

99
00:06:50,319 --> 00:06:51,680
You worked so hard to save her.

100
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,520
A commendation letter
is definitely coming your way.

101
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,600
We really owe that doctor today.

102
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:00,440
Didn't even get her number
to properly thank her.

103
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,960
If she hadn't been there,
we'd have been in real trouble.

104
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,680
Alright, everyone.

105
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,603
Let's get our drinks poured, shall we?

106
00:07:09,603 --> 00:07:12,356
Let's all raise a glass to today.

107
00:07:12,356 --> 00:07:16,280
And then we'll have Mr. Fu say the final words.

108
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,240
There's only one rule tonight.

109
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,439
Eat well.

110
00:07:22,439 --> 00:07:23,880
Drink well.

111
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,041
Cheers.

112
00:07:26,041 --> 00:07:27,320
Thank you.

113
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:30,240
Come on, eat and drink your fill.

114
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,120
Eat well, drink well.

115
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,360
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

116
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,640
To everyone. Enjoy the meal.

117
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,640
Thank you.

118
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,880
- Such a great evening.
- Seriously.

119
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,120
I feel like eating...

120
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,319
Our ride's here. We'll head off.

121
00:07:41,319 --> 00:07:44,199
- Bye.
- Bye.

122
00:07:44,199 --> 00:07:46,400
How are you getting home?

123
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,400
Ruan, where do you live? I can give you a lift.

124
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,160
No, thank you. I'll take her.

125
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,920
Alright then. I'm off.

126
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,639
Actually, it's not that far.

127
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:56,480
I'd like to walk home.

128
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:59,800
Funny, I was thinking the same thing.

129
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:04,400
Alright then, I'll head off. Stay safe.

130
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,920
Yu, come with me.

131
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,520
- Bye, mentor.
- Bye.

132
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,532
Mr. Fu, Ruan. I'll be going now.

133
00:08:09,532 --> 00:08:11,063
Okay, bye.

134
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:54,640
[Great Michelin. Let's come together someday.]
[Almost done here. Where are you?]

135
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:21,080
I thought Jiang was quite lovely today.

136
00:09:22,886 --> 00:09:24,646
How so?

137
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,280
I've flown with her a few times before,

138
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:31,960
but I always felt like
she had some issue with me.

139
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:33,360
Today was different.

140
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:37,000
It felt like when we first met.

141
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:43,360
"If only life could be still at the very moment
when we met for the first time"?

142
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,722
Some first meetings are better left forgotten.

143
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:01,160
Two orders of sea worm rice bowls.

144
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,840
Coming right up!

145
00:10:19,769 --> 00:10:22,080
Didn't you get enough to eat tonight?

146
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:25,320
Did anyone at that table
look like they ate their fill?

147
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:33,665
So if I hadn't shown up tonight,
everyone would've eaten better?

148
00:10:33,665 --> 00:10:35,280
Mr. Fu,

149
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:39,200
sometimes you're surprisingly self-aware.

150
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,560
Want some?

151
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,553
I suggest you try it.

152
00:10:47,553 --> 00:10:49,433
It's really delicious.

153
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,320
So?

154
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:08,520
I've never had it before.

155
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,966
But it's not bad.

156
00:11:10,966 --> 00:11:13,486
Stop it.

157
00:11:18,194 --> 00:11:19,698
Today,

158
00:11:19,698 --> 00:11:23,846
nobody in the back knew
what was happening in the cockpit.

159
00:11:23,846 --> 00:11:26,040
They all thought
it was just another routine landing.

160
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:30,720
But only Yu and I knew
how incredible my mentor was up there.

161
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:35,291
I don't think anyone else
could've handled it that perfectly.

162
00:11:35,291 --> 00:11:39,852
The craziest part is,
after we landed, she was so calm,

163
00:11:39,852 --> 00:11:42,046
like nothing had happened.

164
00:11:42,046 --> 00:11:43,692
Totally unfazed.

165
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,720
Your mentor really is something.

166
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,240
She's been your instructor for a while now.

167
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,520
Do you know her well?

168
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,480
Of course I do.

169
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:02,804
I seem to recall that before I came to
Hengshi Air, she had a similar heroic moment.

170
00:12:02,804 --> 00:12:06,000
- Do you remember?
- Everyone in the industry knew about it.

171
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,920
That's how I first learned about Captain Fan.

172
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:13,160
Do you remember what happened after?

173
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,680
After?

174
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:17,860
She became a celebrity captain,
then an instructor.

175
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,120
Now she's my mentor.

176
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:20,680
Why?

177
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,720
Nothing.

178
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:31,120
I was thinking,
people as brilliant as Captain Fan

179
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:35,360
might carry a lot of weight that nobody sees.

180
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:41,080
In other words, maybe the outcome they get
doesn't always match what they put in.

181
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,850
Isn't that the charm of this profession?

182
00:12:43,850 --> 00:12:48,560
I'm probably not at her level yet,
so I can't really feel it.

183
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,313
I'll have to earn the left seat
of a domestically built aircraft

184
00:12:51,313 --> 00:12:53,513
before I can truly understand.

185
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,720
I do have a question for you.

186
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:07,200
If I hadn't offered you
double the signing bonus,

187
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,440
would you still have chosen Hengshi Air?

188
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,360
Let me tell you,

189
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:14,920
Yan An's sitting at Bo'ao Air
with double the bonus waiting for me.

190
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,720
Take it or leave it.

191
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:18,200
Yan An?

192
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:21,320
But does Yan An have the Z101,
that domestically built large aircraft?

193
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,480
No.

194
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,320
But maybe in a couple of years they will.

195
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:28,280
And does Yan An have Captain Fan
as your instructor?

196
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:29,840
No, they don't.

197
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:33,400
So then, Ms. Ruan,

198
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:37,720
don't you think
you could go a little easier on me?

199
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,680
Have I been hard on you?

200
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:47,880
But seriously,
thank you for the double bonus, Mr. Fu.

201
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:52,200
With that, I can save up a bit more

202
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,280
and finally buy a place.

203
00:14:00,247 --> 00:14:05,240
I've asked Captain Fan about that.

204
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:08,680
Don't take it the wrong way.
Just a standard employee background check.

205
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:11,360
I know you sold your old house.

206
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,159
<i>So the contract is signed.</i>

207
00:14:21,159 --> 00:14:23,840
<i>We'll go through the transfer process next.</i>

208
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:30,000
<i>Can I stay here for a little while longer?</i>

209
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,879
<i>- Of course.
- Thank you.</i>

210
00:14:31,879 --> 00:14:34,000
<i>I'll lock up when I leave.</i>

211
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,120
<i>- Alright.
- Alright then.</i>

212
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,360
<i>We'll be going then, Ms. Ruan.</i>

213
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,720
<i>You little troublemaker.</i>

214
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:16,440
<i>Old Ruan! Your wife is picking on me again.</i>

215
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,440
<i>Let me see.</i>

216
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,640
<i>Look at your messy little face.</i>

217
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,160
<i>Don't bother your mom.</i>

218
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,200
<i>Hurry up and eat.</i>

219
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,736
<i>You too, eat up.</i>

220
00:15:24,736 --> 00:15:26,120
<i>Breakfast time!</i>

221
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,080
<i>I'll make your mom stand in the corner later.</i>

222
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:30,320
<i>Come on, have your breakfast.</i>

223
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,840
<i>Here, wipe your hands.
We're running out of time. Eat up.</i>

224
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,960
<i>Or you'll be late for school.</i>

225
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,559
<i>Sweetie, listen.</i>

226
00:15:36,559 --> 00:15:39,560
<i>- You can't just eat meat and skip the veggies.
- Why not?</i>

227
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:42,280
<i>If so, you won't be able to, you know, go.</i>

228
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,519
<i>I go just fine!</i>

229
00:15:43,519 --> 00:15:46,198
<i>Come on, yesterday you were straining.</i>

230
00:15:46,198 --> 00:15:47,838
<i>Eat up.</i>

231
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,240
<i>Sorry, I need to go.</i>

232
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,399
<i>Go ahead.</i>

233
00:15:54,399 --> 00:15:56,120
<i>We're almost late. Hurry!</i>

234
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,560
<i>Dad, are you done yet?</i>

235
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:04,960
<i>Almost!</i>

236
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,840
<i>Hurry up! I'm going to be late.</i>

237
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,800
<i>Coming!</i>

238
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:12,360
<i>You told me to eat my veggies,
but you're taking forever in the bathroom.</i>

239
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:15,524
<i>It's fine. If you're late today,
tell them your dad overslept.</i>

240
00:16:15,524 --> 00:16:17,920
<i>But the first class is yours.</i>

241
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:18,921
<i>No.</i>

242
00:16:18,921 --> 00:16:20,400
<i>I have an open class today.</i>

243
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,680
<i>I totally forgot.</i>

244
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,680
<i>Let's go!</i>

245
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:26,320
<i>Your face isn't even wiped!</i>

246
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,800
<i>Are you going to school like this?</i>

247
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,240
<i>Hurry up.</i>

248
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:44,680
<i>- That hurts!
- Did I hurt you?</i>

249
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:47,000
<i>- You don't know how to do hair at all!
- I practiced.</i>

250
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,471
<i>You call that "practiced"?</i>

251
00:16:48,471 --> 00:16:51,400
<i>Never mind, I'll do it myself.
I'm off to school.</i>

252
00:18:13,004 --> 00:18:14,564
Mr. Fu.

253
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:21,320
Sometimes poorly-timed comfort
is nothing but salt in the wound.

254
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,840
I'm sorry.

255
00:18:27,604 --> 00:18:29,760
Not eating?

256
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:31,760
Then I'll finish it all myself.

257
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,960
- Good evening, purser.
- Good evening, purser.

258
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,839
<i>Sorry, the subscriber you dialed
can not be connected for the moment,</i>

259
00:18:53,839 --> 00:18:56,042
<i>please redial later.</i>

260
00:18:56,042 --> 00:18:58,742
<i>Sorry, the subscriber you dialed can not--</i>

261
00:19:18,987 --> 00:19:20,279
<i>I'm home.</i>

262
00:19:20,279 --> 00:19:21,519
<i>You must be tired today.</i>

263
00:19:21,519 --> 00:19:23,560
<i>Get some rest early.</i>

264
00:19:58,097 --> 00:20:00,040
Wait...

265
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:02,200
Right here in this courtyard.

266
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,560
Your old house is up there?

267
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:09,760
It's not mine yet.

268
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:13,360
But soon, it'll be mine again.

269
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,320
How so?

270
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,160
Thanks to your generosity, Mr. Fu.

271
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:21,120
That signing bonus was pretty decent.

272
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:22,320
Unfortunately,

273
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:26,480
this area got rezoned for a school district,
so it's still a bit out of reach.

274
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:30,600
Just a few more paychecks
and I should be able to get it.

275
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,920
Come on, let me show you.

276
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,480
See that window?

277
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,960
I lived there for 20 years.

278
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:54,640
That spot right in front of it
used to have our dining table.

279
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:59,440
My dad and I would have breakfast there
every morning.

280
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,360
What's wrong?

281
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:12,560
Nothing.

282
00:21:18,519 --> 00:21:22,800
I'll make it back here someday.

283
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,529
I've said too much tonight.

284
00:21:30,529 --> 00:21:32,009
Let's go.

285
00:21:57,029 --> 00:21:59,360
Mr. Fu, I'm off.

286
00:22:00,382 --> 00:22:02,222
Ruan Si Xian.

287
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,520
Yes?

288
00:22:07,533 --> 00:22:09,254
Nothing.

289
00:22:09,254 --> 00:22:10,774
Good night.

290
00:22:11,861 --> 00:22:13,341
Good night.

291
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:05,040
[Notice Regarding the Handling of
Hengshi Air Flight SH2076 Emergency Incident]

292
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:10,080
<i>Your mentor really is something.</i>

293
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:13,400
<i>Do you remember what happened after?</i>

294
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:16,599
<i>After? She became a celebrity captain,
then an instructor.</i>

295
00:23:16,599 --> 00:23:17,800
<i>Now she's my mentor.</i>

296
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,400
<i>Why?</i>

297
00:23:20,473 --> 00:23:21,480
<i>Nothing.</i>

298
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,360
<i>Ruan Si Xian.</i>

299
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,960
<i>Yes?</i>

300
00:23:26,345 --> 00:23:27,905
<i>Nothing.</i>

301
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:42,760
- What...
- Manager Wang.

302
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:45,503
I'm sorry. I was in a hurry.

303
00:23:45,503 --> 00:23:47,680
You're always charging around.

304
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:50,200
- Where are you going?
- Manager Wang, have you heard?

305
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,359
My mentor's been grounded.

306
00:23:51,359 --> 00:23:52,800
There's got to be some mistake.

307
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,185
Then what are you planning to do?

308
00:23:54,185 --> 00:23:56,040
I need to talk to our group captain.

309
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:58,200
Hold on. Wait a minute.

310
00:23:59,514 --> 00:24:00,921
Come with me.

311
00:24:00,921 --> 00:24:02,600
Come on. Sit over there.

312
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:04,880
I'll get you some water.

313
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,840
- Sit down.
- I don't have time for this.

314
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,480
I have to go.

315
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,759
What's the rush?

316
00:24:09,759 --> 00:24:11,640
I know exactly what's going on.

317
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:13,680
I know what you're about to say.

318
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:19,280
That's why I pulled you aside
to get you to calm down.

319
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:21,240
Sit right there and don't move.

320
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:25,473
The company knows what it's doing.

321
00:24:25,473 --> 00:24:27,800
This whole thing is temporary.

322
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,400
Why are you getting so worked up?

323
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:31,680
But being grounded is a big deal.

324
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:34,240
My mentor didn't do anything wrong yesterday.

325
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:37,306
The plane landed safely,
the passenger got medical care on time,

326
00:24:37,306 --> 00:24:39,160
and Mr. Fu even bought the whole crew dinner.

327
00:24:39,160 --> 00:24:41,480
I know all of that.

328
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:44,440
And if you go to your group captain,
he can't do anything either.

329
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,480
Fine.

330
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,960
Then I won't go to him.

331
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,520
Then I'll go straight to Mr. Fu and ask him,

332
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:50,559
the thank-you from last night,
or the penalty this morning,

333
00:24:50,559 --> 00:24:52,400
which is it?

334
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:53,880
That won't change a thing.

335
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,440
This is a company decision.

336
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:59,400
We're all on Captain Fan's side emotionally.

337
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:02,800
But the company
has its safety assessment system.

338
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:06,400
Once it's triggered,
the pilot gets grounded for investigation.

339
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:09,480
But the system is not set in stone.

340
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:11,240
It's made by humans.

341
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:14,200
Besides, my mentor saved a life.
She should be commended, not punished.

342
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,720
Is Fu Ming Yu that blind to right and wrong?

343
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:18,279
Ruan Si Xian, let me be straight with you.

344
00:25:18,279 --> 00:25:19,559
First thing this morning,

345
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:22,680
Captain Fan herself accepted the decision.

346
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:23,839
If you kick up a fuss right now,

347
00:25:23,839 --> 00:25:27,020
are you doing her a favor,
or just making things more difficult for her?

348
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:33,880
Sit right there and finish this glass of water.

349
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:36,440
Think it through.

350
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,480
And you're not leaving till it's empty.

351
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:05,303
No. I totally feel this one.

352
00:26:05,303 --> 00:26:07,079
You work your tail off all day,

353
00:26:07,079 --> 00:26:09,280
and instead of a thank-you,

354
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,320
they tell you to
hand over your badge and leave?

355
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:14,120
- That's just wrong.
- Right?

356
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,560
To me, it's a total slap in the face.

357
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:20,000
And last night, I was like an idiot,
strolling down the street with him,

358
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,360
pouring my heart out about
buying back my house.

359
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:23,920
I thought we were friends,

360
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:26,319
but he's ready to put his employees
at the bottom of the pile.

361
00:26:26,319 --> 00:26:28,800
Hold up. I have a question.

362
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:32,600
Since when have you two been friends?

363
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:34,840
Is that the point?

364
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:39,520
You're not taking his side on this, are you?

365
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:42,640
When have I ever taken his side?

366
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:45,839
I'm just being objective.

367
00:26:45,839 --> 00:26:47,760
Mr. Fu's the vice president.

368
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:50,480
Anything that lands on his desk,
he's got to sign.

369
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:54,320
That doesn't mean
he's happy about every single one of them.

370
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:57,868
Otherwise, why did he have
that look on his face last night?

371
00:26:57,868 --> 00:27:00,000
Like he had something to say but couldn't?

372
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:03,560
So he grounds my mentor,
and I'm supposed to feel sorry for him now?

373
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:06,040
Wait, don't drag me into this.

374
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,800
I'm innocent.

375
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:12,360
I think the really innocent one
is Ruan's mentor, Captain Fan.

376
00:27:12,360 --> 00:27:16,080
She did the right thing,
yet she's the one paying for it.

377
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:20,440
Your phone's ringing.

378
00:27:24,119 --> 00:27:25,880
It's my mentor.

379
00:27:29,457 --> 00:27:31,185
Hello, mentor?

380
00:27:31,185 --> 00:27:34,920
<i>Ruan, you're off tomorrow. Got any plans?</i>

381
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:37,080
No.

382
00:27:39,595 --> 00:27:42,720
Slow down! Watch yourself!

383
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,360
Thanks for giving up your day off
to help me with the kid.

384
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:48,680
I owe you one.

385
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:52,280
I didn't realize
Lu Lu was already in full-time daycare.

386
00:27:54,247 --> 00:27:56,920
Well, her grandparents aren't retired yet.

387
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,600
That's just how it is
when both parents are pilots.

388
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:01,040
But honestly,
this might be a blessing in disguise.

389
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:03,680
I haven't taken her out to play in forever.

390
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:09,560
But I still don't think it's fair.

391
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:12,680
What would be fair, then?

392
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:14,960
Didn't the patient get timely treatment?

393
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:18,920
Yeah, but we didn't do anything wrong,
and you still got penalized.

394
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:22,720
And even if someone had to take the fall,
it shouldn't all be on you.

395
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:24,200
If not me, then who?

396
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:26,840
I'm the captain in command.

397
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:31,040
The day you're sitting in that seat,
you'll do the same.

398
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:41,600
You know why I recommended you
to the Aviation Academy back then?

399
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:46,560
Wasn't it because I kept pushing you
until you finally gave in?

400
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:49,520
But you still had to convince me.

401
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:52,976
And back then,
the academy only took sponsored pilots.

402
00:28:52,976 --> 00:28:55,190
Then why?

403
00:28:55,190 --> 00:29:00,400
I remember telling you
every single challenge female pilots face.

404
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:04,720
Anyone else would have
weighed the pros and cons and walked.

405
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:06,525
But you didn't.

406
00:29:06,525 --> 00:29:09,520
You came back and told me
you'd made your choice.

407
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:14,920
You'd sell your house, pay your own tuition,
whatever it took.

408
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:18,760
Around that time, I'd just had the baby.

409
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:21,606
Everyone at home wanted me
to quit and be a full-time mom.

410
00:29:21,606 --> 00:29:24,320
And I was burnt out too.

411
00:29:24,320 --> 00:29:26,720
I was ready to hand in my resignation.

412
00:29:27,563 --> 00:29:29,763
But then you showed up.

413
00:29:31,619 --> 00:29:35,800
I suddenly saw myself back
when I first started flying.

414
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:40,680
That passion came flooding back.

415
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:47,079
So in a way, I gave you a leg up,
but you also gave me one.

416
00:29:47,079 --> 00:29:49,440
But when it happened, I froze.

417
00:29:49,440 --> 00:29:51,720
You didn't hesitate to save that passenger,

418
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:54,080
and I tried to hold you back.

419
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:59,000
We all know a bank angle over 30 degrees
triggers the QAR warning.

420
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:03,880
But a steep bank with autopilot off
buys the patient more time,

421
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,480
so I think it's worth it.

422
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:07,146
There's nothing to be afraid of.

423
00:30:07,146 --> 00:30:13,200
As pilots, we put our passengers' lives
and safety above everything else.

424
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,439
I'd do it again without hesitation.

425
00:30:15,439 --> 00:30:17,120
And I don't regret it.

426
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:20,000
Whether you and Yu tried to
persuade me or stop me,

427
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:22,140
I know you meant well.

428
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:25,279
But sticking to the rulebook

429
00:30:25,279 --> 00:30:29,560
is exactly what you two should be doing
at this stage.

430
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:35,000
And the minute I gave that order,
I already knew what was coming.

431
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,640
I still chose to do it.

432
00:30:36,640 --> 00:30:39,720
That means I was ready to face
whatever came next.

433
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:41,560
So don't be too hard on yourselves.

434
00:30:41,560 --> 00:30:44,701
And don't go arguing with Mr. Fu on my account.

435
00:30:44,701 --> 00:30:46,480
After all,

436
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:50,795
this kind of call
isn't his alone to make anyway.

437
00:30:50,795 --> 00:30:53,416
We saved a life.

438
00:30:53,416 --> 00:30:55,999
A kid still has her mom.

439
00:30:55,999 --> 00:30:58,400
That honestly makes me happy.

440
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,880
Truly.

441
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:05,920
Mentor...

442
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:07,640
I'm sorry.

443
00:31:08,440 --> 00:31:10,720
I have to be honest.

444
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:14,359
I thought about going to appeal for you.

445
00:31:14,359 --> 00:31:18,200
But they said it would just make things worse.

446
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:20,000
And...

447
00:31:20,796 --> 00:31:23,880
I backed off.

448
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,319
I feel like a coward.

449
00:31:25,319 --> 00:31:29,440
Ruan, at that moment,
I had all those passengers behind me

450
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:31,000
and barely any time.

451
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,560
I had to decide right then and there.

452
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:35,360
You have to remember,

453
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:38,240
we shall see every passenger back there

454
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:42,666
our parent, our grandparent, or our sibling.

455
00:31:42,666 --> 00:31:47,683
Maybe they're heading home, or to a reunion,

456
00:31:47,683 --> 00:31:50,080
or chasing a dream or love.

457
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:53,600
Our job is to get them there safe and sound.

458
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:56,400
That's our highest mission.

459
00:31:59,116 --> 00:32:01,036
I get it, mentor.

460
00:32:37,338 --> 00:32:38,819
Morning.

461
00:32:38,819 --> 00:32:41,220
Morning, Mr. Yan.

462
00:32:41,220 --> 00:32:43,220
Are you flying today?

463
00:32:46,635 --> 00:32:47,676
Jump in.

464
00:32:47,676 --> 00:32:50,757
I'm on the way to the airport base.
Just passing by.

465
00:32:52,089 --> 00:32:54,992
We said we'd still be friends, right?

466
00:32:54,992 --> 00:32:56,200
And it is on my way, really.

467
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,800
No, it's not that.

468
00:32:57,800 --> 00:33:01,720
I just called a taxi. It should be here soon.

469
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,800
I've been watching you for a while.

470
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:06,920
You haven't gotten one.

471
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:12,440
Mr. Yan, it doesn't look like
you're "just passing by."

472
00:33:13,719 --> 00:33:16,066
Don't call me out like that.

473
00:33:16,066 --> 00:33:18,946
Come on, get in. You don't want to be late.

474
00:33:20,287 --> 00:33:22,680
Alright then. Thanks.

475
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:24,120
Let's go.

476
00:33:26,422 --> 00:33:27,942
Watch your head.

477
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,960
If you have something to say, just say it.

478
00:34:01,569 --> 00:34:07,440
Ruan Si Xian, I never properly apologized for
what happened before.

479
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:08,800
I'm sorry.

480
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,360
That's in the past.

481
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:12,800
Let's drop it.

482
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:14,400
Just tell me what's on your mind.

483
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:16,840
To be honest,

484
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:23,320
did you turn me down because of Fu Ming Yu?

485
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:27,720
Don't even bother answering.

486
00:34:27,720 --> 00:34:32,199
He's been bad-mouthing me left and right,

487
00:34:32,199 --> 00:34:36,119
making me look bad so he can swoop in himself.

488
00:34:36,119 --> 00:34:37,639
Is that all you wanted to say?

489
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:40,599
No, there's more. I've thought it through.

490
00:34:40,599 --> 00:34:42,599
If he's going to play dirty, so will I.

491
00:34:42,599 --> 00:34:46,309
Trade dirt? I've got plenty.

492
00:34:46,309 --> 00:34:49,760
When in fourth grade, Fu Ming Yu
went to the bathroom without toilet paper.

493
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:52,360
Stuck in there for over two hours.
Legs went completely numb.

494
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,522
I had to bring him some toilet paper.

495
00:34:54,522 --> 00:34:57,840
I've got a ton of stories like that.

496
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:59,559
He messed things up for me?

497
00:34:59,559 --> 00:35:01,519
Fine. Then nobody gets a free pass.

498
00:35:01,519 --> 00:35:04,440
If you want to hear more,
I've got plenty of dirt on him.

499
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:08,800
I can start from kindergarten.

500
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:17,840
- I know.
- Like that one...

501
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:21,340
- That smug little grin, remember?
- Yes, I do!

502
00:35:21,960 --> 00:35:23,639
I saw that too.

503
00:35:23,639 --> 00:35:24,760
Sorry.

504
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:27,120
You didn't even open your suitcase?

505
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:28,320
Did that really happen?

506
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:30,160
Really. Why would I make that up?

507
00:35:30,160 --> 00:35:32,800
- Unbelievable.
- Call me later. Bye.

508
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,360
Bye.

509
00:35:35,860 --> 00:35:37,701
Showing up to work in person, Mr. Fu?

510
00:35:37,701 --> 00:35:39,661
Picking up a side gig as a driver now?

511
00:36:01,176 --> 00:36:03,176
He's really something else!

512
00:36:04,920 --> 00:36:07,000
Where were we?

513
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:10,360
We were talking about Captain Fan.
Maintenance has done their checks.

514
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:14,160
The landing was a bit overweight,
but the aircraft's fine.

515
00:36:14,160 --> 00:36:16,960
I've gone over it back and forth
with the Safety Committee,

516
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:19,080
and the answer keeps coming back the same.

517
00:36:19,080 --> 00:36:21,640
It exceeded the QAR parameters.

518
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:25,799
Honestly, I've always thought
the system itself is flawed.

519
00:36:25,799 --> 00:36:29,800
The QAR is just a data recorder,

520
00:36:29,800 --> 00:36:34,719
but the company tightened the thresholds
way beyond what's really necessary for safety,

521
00:36:34,719 --> 00:36:37,040
just to make management easier.

522
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:39,960
Over the years, pilots flying perfectly safely
still got penalized

523
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:44,400
for exceeding the QAR parameters by a hair.

524
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:47,760
So you think it's unfair.

525
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:54,131
It's okay, you can say it.

526
00:36:54,131 --> 00:36:56,880
I think it's more than unfair.

527
00:36:56,880 --> 00:37:00,419
The company's QAR oversight is way too strict.

528
00:37:00,419 --> 00:37:06,320
If you ask me, overcompliance
means nothing but lazy management.

529
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:14,521
Zhu Dong, I'm glad to hear you say that.

530
00:37:14,521 --> 00:37:18,840
But for the company,
this is a major reform we have to face.

531
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,040
Reform is a big deal.

532
00:37:21,040 --> 00:37:24,680
You haven't been at Hengshi Air long.
Don't stir up too much trouble.

533
00:37:24,680 --> 00:37:28,565
Spending time and energy
on something pointless,

534
00:37:28,565 --> 00:37:30,480
that's what I call stirring up trouble.

535
00:37:31,125 --> 00:37:36,560
Right now, our priority is to
sort out Captain Fan's matter properly.

536
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:48,480
What are you doing here?

537
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:50,080
Waiting for you.

538
00:38:50,080 --> 00:38:51,920
For what?

539
00:39:00,923 --> 00:39:05,483
Why were you with Yan An today?

540
00:39:11,219 --> 00:39:12,544
What?

541
00:39:13,447 --> 00:39:16,160
Why were you in his car?

542
00:39:17,362 --> 00:39:19,241
He gave me a ride.

543
00:39:19,241 --> 00:39:20,607
What?

544
00:39:20,607 --> 00:39:23,448
Do I need to report that to you?

545
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:26,360
Why?

546
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:28,920
I said he gave me a ride
because it was on his way.

547
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:31,680
If you've had too much to drink,
go home and sleep.

548
00:39:42,800 --> 00:39:44,080
Let go.

549
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:45,960
Are you going to tell me
who I can hang out with?

550
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:47,480
Don't you think you're crossing a line?

551
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:49,480
You're my boss.

552
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:52,360
Are you going to manage my life too?

553
00:39:53,846 --> 00:39:57,480
Unless you don't want to be my boss,

554
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:59,640
but want to be my boyfriend instead?

555
00:40:01,679 --> 00:40:03,640
In your dreams.

556
00:40:31,600 --> 00:40:33,120
- Hello.
- Hello.

557
00:40:33,120 --> 00:40:34,840
I have an appointment with Mr. Fu.

558
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,080
Mr. Fu is in a meeting right now.

559
00:40:36,080 --> 00:40:39,160
Would you like to wait inside?

560
00:40:45,119 --> 00:40:46,720
Please, have a seat.

561
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:50,840
Have some water.

562
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,320
<i>The first love returned after years abroad?</i>

563
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:06,520
Got that booked?

564
00:41:06,520 --> 00:41:09,760
Yes, don't worry. It's all set.

565
00:41:11,199 --> 00:41:14,159
- Fu Ming Yu, Mr. Fu.
- What are you doing here?

566
00:41:14,159 --> 00:41:15,200
My new proposal.

567
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:17,320
I've been working on it for a week.

568
00:41:17,320 --> 00:41:18,840
I guarantee you'll be satisfied.

569
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:22,400
Mr. Fu, Instructor Fang is waiting for you
at the training center.

570
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:25,072
I'm swamped today.
You might have to wait a while.

571
00:41:25,072 --> 00:41:27,480
- Let's go.
- Of course.

572
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:33,280
How long... is "a while"?

573
00:41:36,760 --> 00:41:39,080
<i>Merely a contractor.</i>

574
00:41:39,833 --> 00:41:47,240
That's my story of how I became a pilot
at Hengshi Air.

575
00:41:47,240 --> 00:41:50,280
I hope it helps.

576
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:51,840
Thank you.

577
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:02,360
Honestly, I'd love to come
to Baidao University again

578
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:06,840
to talk more about single-pilot operations
and fully automated flight.

579
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:09,240
And next time, I could bring along
a colleague of mine.

580
00:42:09,240 --> 00:42:11,080
Her name is Ruan Si Xian.

581
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:12,840
She's also a Baidao graduate.

582
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:14,360
Your senior.

583
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:16,920
When I first met her, I was curious.

584
00:42:16,920 --> 00:42:20,470
What kind of school produces a pilot like that?

585
00:42:20,470 --> 00:42:23,721
And after being here today, I get it.

586
00:42:23,721 --> 00:42:25,464
You're all amazing.

587
00:42:25,464 --> 00:42:30,400
I really wish I'd had the chance
to spend four years at a place like this.

588
00:42:30,400 --> 00:42:36,000
There's still some time left,
and I'm sure you all have questions.

589
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:40,520
Go ahead, feel free to ask.

590
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:44,600
Yes, the young man over there.

591
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:46,080
Captain Yue, I'd like to ask,

592
00:42:46,080 --> 00:42:49,840
once you become a captain,
does finding a partner get any easier?

593
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:54,480
I can give you a straight answer.

594
00:42:54,480 --> 00:42:59,720
<i>I think there's a common misconception
about pilots.</i>

595
00:42:59,720 --> 00:43:04,307
<i>I can't speak for other airlines, but at ours,
a lot of pilots are still single.</i>

596
00:43:04,307 --> 00:43:05,960
<i>Our circle is really small.</i>

597
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:07,986
<i>We're either flying or resting.</i>

598
00:43:07,986 --> 00:43:10,960
<i>We don't have much time
to focus on personal matters.</i>

599
00:43:10,960 --> 00:43:12,320
<i>- Thank you.
- What about you?</i>

600
00:43:12,320 --> 00:43:14,400
<i>Are you single too?</i>

601
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:20,440
<i>I am.</i>

602
00:43:20,440 --> 00:43:22,000
<i>Still working on that one.</i>

603
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:23,360
<i>Haven't cracked it yet.</i>

604
00:43:23,360 --> 00:43:24,840
<i>That's great!</i>

605
00:43:24,840 --> 00:43:26,520
<i>That's great!</i>

